Compiled terminfo fixtures for terminfo_test.go
===============================================

terminfo/70/* are compiled terminfo entries, committed so that the tests do
not need tic. They were generated on macOS 26 with ncurses 6.0.20150808 tic,
whose xterm-256color entry the first three "use=". The source is
terminfo.src.

Legacy format (magic 0432, 16-bit numbers):

    tic -x -o testdata/terminfo testdata/terminfo.src

  pst-present    xterm-256color + Pst              extended section, Pst set
  pst-absent     xterm-256color                    extended section, no Pst
  pst-cancelled  pst-present with Pst@             extended section, Pst cancelled (-2)
  pst-plain      a few standard capabilities       no extended section
  pst-only       Pst and two standard capabilities extended section with one string

Extended number format (magic 01036, 32-bit numbers). ncurses 6.0 tic cannot
write it, so these were converted from the legacy files with gen32.go, which
widens every number field and leaves everything else byte-for-byte the same:

    for n in present absent cancelled plain; do
      go run testdata/gen32.go testdata/terminfo/70/pst-$n testdata/terminfo/70/pst-$n-32
    done

tic writes into hexadecimal subdirectories (70 is "p") on macOS. The tests
copy entries into a letter subdirectory (p/) at test time to cover that
layout too.
